      "id": "split",
      "title": "Cut like a shell",
      "plain": "The guard cuts it where a shell would; the git push inside the quoted message stays words.",
      "technical": "splitCommand cuts on unquoted &&, ;, | and expands bash -c; the quoted -m message is one word, so its git push is never a push.",
      "focus": [
        "segments"
      ],
      "flows": [
        "split"
      ],
      "ms": 3600
    },
    {
      "id": "where",
      "title": "Where each one runs",
      "plain": "It follows the folder along the chain: git -C moves one command, cd moves the rest.",
      "technical": "trackCwd gives each segment its cwd: git -C moves only its own, cd every one after; repoState reads that folder's branch and rules.",
      "focus": [
